-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ד/2 — החלטות ועדת המעקב מיום 28.5.2013 להסכם עוז לתמורה (29.12.2013)
-- The circular publishes the steering committee's decision of 28.5.2013
-- to the Oz LaTmura agreement of 14.8.2011, in its own order: its §§1–18
-- are the decision's §§1, 15, 2–14 and 16–18, word for word or nearly so.
-- A circular that carries an agreement's rule imports it (MMS-521, MMS-591):
-- the rules are the decision's, `2013-05-28_oz-latmura_vaadat-higui-decision`,
-- and the founding agreement's sections it amends, `oz-founding-<N>`; each
-- row below that publishes one names the rule that encodes it there.
--
-- What the circular says of its own, and so what this file encodes:
--   * §12 ¶2: by a steering-committee decision of 24.12.2013 (not in the
--     corpus), §12 (the decision's §11: the transition supplement's base,
--     its training-fund contributions and the 1987 transition supplement)
--     governs from the start of the reform, where the decision gives it no
--     day and so governs from its own (convention dates.undated-amendment,
--     whose exception this is);
--   * §12 ¶3: the transition supplement only while employed on the
--     reform's terms as a principal, which is how the decision's rules
--     already read it;
--   * §9: two worked examples of the new §17(ד) table, held against the
--     decision's rule.
-- What it leaves out: the decision's §8(א) (the floors in §17(א)'s table
-- now "not fewer than §17(ד) says") and its §19, of which §19 says
-- instructions will follow in a separate circular. Neither omission is a
-- rule: the decision's rules stand as the decision gives them.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT conventions
IMPORT `oz-founding-common`
IMPORT `oz-founding-15`
IMPORT `oz-founding-20`
IMPORT `oz-founding-24`
IMPORT `oz-founding-38`
IMPORT `oz-founding-39`
IMPORT `2013-05-28_oz-latmura_vaadat-higui-decision`

-- not weighed against `the Hours of Work and Rest Law`: allocates to role
-- holders a share of the frontal hours of the week tables (at least so many
-- hours): it orders the hours of the agreement's week and adds none.

§ `חוזר תשע"ד/2 החלטות ועדת המעקב לעוז לתמורה`

-- not weighed against `the Equal Opportunities Law`: §14 raises the
-- largest position of a mother teacher in the Oz agreement's partial
-- implementation (§26(ו) and (ו1)); she is the one the earlier agreements
-- define (the Oz agreement's §11(ג)), the mother teacher of the takanon's §1.13.1 (and of
-- the base agreement's §7(ג) in the reform), and the fathers it leaves out
-- of §4(א) are weighed there, on the card mother-position-fathers
-- (F-1.13-e, F-ofek-hadash-base-7-c).

-- akn:preamble The letterhead, date, reference, addressee and subject line; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p13 The subject repeated as a heading; no rule.
-- akn:preamble/p14 The decision's own opening (its ¶2): the committee of 28.5.2013, under section 59 of the agreement; its power is the decision's F-oz-higui-2013-a.
-- akn:preamble/p15 States the circular's purpose, to publish the decisions; no rule.

